msgctxt "64"
msgid ""
"Whaddya want this time? Sorry, but I'm not in the mood to\r\n"
"talk about your little land problem."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "76"
msgid "Rikiya told me what's going on with Saki."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "88"
msgid ""
"Ugh, that's Rikiya for ya. Never knows when to keep his damn\r\n"
"mouth shut. This ain't your problem, Kiryu-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "100"
msgid "Why don't you go look for her?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "112"
msgid "Can't. Wouldn't be so miserable if it was that easy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "124"
msgid "What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "136"
msgid ""
"She ran away 'cause she didn't wanna live with me anymore.\r\n"
"I'd just scare her off if I went hunting for her now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "148"
msgid ""
"You don't know that for sure. Why don't you try to figure\r\n"
"out why she really ran away? It wouldn't be too late to\r\n"
"catch up to her if you go now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "160"
msgid ""
"Rikiya told me Saki's mom has been out looking for her\r\n"
"recently. Maybe Saki just wanted to see her again after all\r\n"
"this time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "172"
msgid ""
"Same difference. Either she wants to be with her mom, or she\r\n"
"doesn't wanna be with me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "184"
msgid "God dammit! Am I really worse than that miserable whore!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "196"
msgid "Nakahara..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "208"
msgid ""
"Guess a yakuza like me doesn't have any business taking in\r\n"
"a kid in the first place, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "220"
msgid ""
"That's not true. All children need is someone who really,\r\n"
"truly cares about them. It doesn't matter what you do for\r\n"
"a living."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "232"
msgid ""
"The hell do you know? You think you're some kinda kid expert\r\n"
"just 'cause you run a fucking orphanage!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "244"
msgid "I know enough. I was an orphan myself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "256"
msgid "Huh!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "268"
msgid "Not only that, the man who raised me was in the yakuza."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "280"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "292"
msgid ""
"And since I have no memories of my birth parents, that man\r\n"
"is more of a father than I've ever had. He might have been\r\n"
"a yakuza, yeah... but I loved him all the same."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "304"
msgid ""
"And I'm sure Saki loves you, too. But it's natural for her\r\n"
"to miss her mom. She's still just a kid, after all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "316"
msgid "You... You really think?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "328"
msgid ""
"Of course. Now get out there and find her before someone\r\n"
"else does."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "340"
msgid "But..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "352"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "364"
msgid "I can't."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "376"
msgid "Why not?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "388"
msgid ""
"Look at me, Kiryu-san. Why would Saki ever wanna come back\r\n"
"to this mess after seeing her mother?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "400"
msgid "A thug like me could never compare to an actual parent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "412"
msgid "I'm just gonna have to face the facts. Saki's gone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "424"
msgid "You really think so?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "436"
msgid "Yeah... I do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "448"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "6276"
msgid "Nakahara"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "6280"
msgid "Kiryu"
msgstr ""

